# Mishra's Workshop's mana can only be spent on artifact spells: Bot1 taps the Workshop and two Mox Sapphires with Bot2's
# Duress on the stack and casts Daze for its mana cost {1}{U}, a spell that is not an artifact. The {1} is paid with the
# second Sapphire, not with the Workshop's {C} (which the engine would spend first if it could), so the Workshop's
# {C}{C}{C} is still in the pool afterwards, still restricted.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mishra's Workshop
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Daze
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Duress
Swamp x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mishra's Workshop.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Duress.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mishra's Workshop.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Daze.Cast(Duress)
? Bot1.Mana = {C}{C}{C} (ArtifactSpells)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Duress
Bot1.Graveyard = Daze
